omx-clap-host (0.34.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * test-socket: the host is a client of the test's own PipeWire, through
    PipeWire's libjack
  * test-socket: where /proc is masked, socket_e2e.sh runs as a session of
    its own
  * tests: importing plugin-hostd's client writes no bytecode into
    plugin-hostd's tree
  * test-codes: the reply-codes check reads the host domain, where V15 moved
    HOST_REPLY_CODES
  * Revert the chain-2 fold (V16 + V29, #172): it waits for chain 3
  * the old-home grep: the CLAP plugin features name their user at its new
    home
  * packaging: every floor on a package this delivery releases is its
    delivered version
  * release: omx-clap-core 0.34.0 (the sorting pass)
  * V29: the scan domain's check reads the package as it installs, so the
    verbs meet HOSTING_VERB_HOSTS
  * V16: the host verbs check reads plugin-hostd-protocol's verbs from its
    domain only, and refuses a data file of the package by name
  * V16: a stale 3/plugin-hostd-protocol/verbs.json is refused by the host
    verbs check, a test that fails while it reads it (red)
  * V29: the committed renders of omx-clap follow omx-contract's
    HOSTING_VERB_HOSTS read
  * V16: the host verbs check reads plugin-hostd-protocol's verbs from its
    domain plugin-hostd, through omx-contract's reader
  * V16: the host verbs check reads plugin-hostd-protocol's verbs from its
    domain plugin-hostd, a test that fails while it reads data/verbs.json
    (red)
  * V29: VERB_HOSTS is HOSTING_VERB_HOSTS of omx-clap's hosting data
  * V15: the host verbs check binds the curve in a standard unit id, and the
    lower-case id is refused
  * V25: the comment of host_transport_test.c names omx-dsp's
    ORACLE_FULL_RATES
  * V25: the tests read the oracle rates from omx-dsp's definitions, and
    omx-dsp-devel is the 0.34.0 floor
  * V23d revert: the two stray CI lines go, and the vendor-code checks read
    omx-contract's header, red until it carries them
  * V23d: revert for this chain: the param-contract sheet stays
    omx-contract's, and this tree reads it there
  * V23d: x-file is the data path again (the x-file half of c9a4421
    reverted); the renders follow omx-contract S0 ec71185
  * V15: revert 6dbd6f0, the verbs items name their data file again
  * release-same-pass: plugin-qualify no longer names a
    plugin-qualify-contract
  * ci: plugin-hostd.sh takes a release tag or a branch by name, never a
    commit
  * ci: plugin-hostd is read from main by name; the chain passes its own head
    through the same variable
  * ci: read plugin-hostd's sorting branch by name, as the chain does, not a
    sha pin
  * V27b: the comments that named omx-contract as the source of the CLAP and
    LV2 terms name their domains
  * V15: host_verbs_check.py reads the verbs and reply codes from the
    installed domains
  * V27b: the CLAP header inventory and its coverage check live here, with
    the terms
  * V15: the verbs items name the domain's own document as their data file
  * V27a reader: the scan's field list is held to the LV2 terms of
    plugin-db's lv2 domain
  * V15: the host words and the verbs are the domains host and omx-clap;
    data/verbs.json is gone
  * V23d: the vocabulary renders are as before: omx-contract's S0 keeps an
    installed domain's run-time items out of its owner's render
  * V23d: the committed vocabulary renders carry the scan domain's words, as
    omx-contract renders them now
  * V23d: the mapping names coef for the coefficient unit; the check installs
    omx-contract's own domains
  * V23d: the code sheet's data file is named for its domain, and the header
    banner says where it is rendered from
  * V27b, V23d: drop the transition excludes; name the clap domain in the
    scan's comment
  * V27b: the CLAP terms are the items of the clap domain, and the scan reads
    them there
  * rename: the two checks that named the old header files and the rpm
    library package follow the rename
  * ci: every pull request body closes an issue
  * V1: untrack the scan_panel_words_test binary the previous commit swept
    in, and ignore it
  * V1: omx_clap_ext.h takes the panel words from omx-panel's rendered header
  * V27b: the CLAP domain, with the flag-to-scale mapping (F2)
  * V21: the scale codes are this tree's, mapped to the standard scales (F2);
    the header stops spelling them
  * V23d: the param-contract code sheet is this tree's, with its mapping to
    the standard units (F2)
  * rename: omx-clap-core becomes omx-clap in every package, library and
    install name

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:54:18 +0000
